{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Take the sum, etc.</b> The need for this census now was in order to make known that even though twenty-four thousand had fallen, nevertheless sixty myriads remained, for a complete population exists only when there are sixty myriads, for one does not say the blessing 'Blessed is the wise one of mysteries' except when one sees sixty myriads (B'rakhot 58a). Therefore it came to make known that upon their entry into the land they were a complete population." "And the fact that He sealed upon all the tribes there the name י״ה specifically in this census — for they were not yet suspected of licentiousness until they stumbled at Shittim in licentiousness, and there was room for the nations to say: its end proves about its beginning — just as the males committed harlotry after foreign daughters, so too in Egypt the women committed harlotry and broke loose, because the Egyptians had also dominated their mothers. Therefore it says 'of the Hanochite,' 'of the Palluite,' and He sealed upon them the name י״ה, for this name mediates between man and woman, to indicate that all were born of a man and a woman upon whom the name י״ה was between them. And the precedence of the ה over the י comes to make known the merit of the women, for the ה is given to the woman and the י to the man. And indeed the women were more guarded from forbidden relations than the men, as Scripture publicized Shlomit daughter of Dibri — she alone was wanton, and all the rest were modest (Vayikra Rabbah 32:5). But the men were weeping for their families, on account of forbidden relations that were prohibited to them, and many of them stumbled at Shittim. Therefore He placed the ה of י״ה before the י, for the essential thing that He came to make known was the merit of the women — that the Egyptians had not dominated their mothers. And furthermore, in every seal the letters are reversed, so that they come in their proper order on the thing being sealed; and Israel — they are the seal, as it is written (Song 8:6): ״Set me as a seal upon your heart״, etc. — when I am the seal, then the name י״ה is engraved upon me." "And what He further added the name י״ה in three tribes — and they are the Reubenite, the Simeonite, the Zebulunite: ״These are the families of the Reubenite,״ and likewise for Simeon and Zebulun — for these needed two witnesses more than the rest. For Reuben stumbled in the matter of Bilhah, and from Simeon came forth Zimri. And the matter appears clear that the twenty-four thousand who fell were mostly from Simeon, and the deficiency in the number of this tribe proves it. And Zebulun — ״at the shore of the seas he shall dwell״ (Genesis 49:13), and our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Ketuvot 61a): the marital obligation of sailors is once every six months. And there is reason to be concerned, since those who go down to the sea in ships are separated from their wives, that perhaps through this they may come to licentiousness; therefore He sealed the name י״ה a second time upon all three, to say that all of them are seed blessed by HaShem, and guarded from forbidden relations both for the past and for the future, more than any nation and tongue."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:43:16.498147120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}